---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { GALLERY_RETENTION_MONTHS } from "../../lib/gallery-retention.js";
---

<BaseLayout title="Photo Policy" description="What photos we accept for the Community Gallery, how we protect privacy, and how long we keep them.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Site Info" title="Photo Policy" description="Last updated: October 2026" />
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <div class="prose max-w-none prose-headings:font-display">
      <p>
        We love seeing neighborhood life through your lens. This page covers what we'll post, what we won't, and
        how long we hang on to your photos — which, by design, isn't forever. It applies to the
        <a href="/community-gallery">Community Gallery</a> and to any resident photo we use elsewhere on the site
        or in the newsletter. Every photo has to meet these rules before it goes up; editors check each one.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Only send photos you took yourself.</li>
        <li>Anyone recognizable in the shot has to be OK with it — and for kids, that means a parent or guardian.</li>
        <li>No house numbers, license plates, or other details that point to a specific home or person.</li>
        <li>Gallery photos come down after {GALLERY_RETENTION_MONTHS} months, or sooner if you ask.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we're looking for</h2>
      <p>
        Photos from in and around Bent Grass that fit one of the gallery's categories: local events, local
        critters, local weather, and everyday neighborhood scenes. Shots taken from public spaces, common areas, or
        your own property are best.
      </p>

      <h2>What we won't post</h2>
      <p>We'll decline (or ask to crop or blur) any photo that includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>People who haven't said yes.</strong> If someone is recognizable, they need to be OK with the photo
          being online. Crowds at a public event where no one is the focus are fine.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Identifiable children without a parent or guardian's OK.</strong> Even with permission, we won't
          post kids' names, schools, or anything that ties a child to a specific home.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Details that identify a home or person</strong> — house numbers, license plates, mail, people
          visible through windows, or security cameras and keypads.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Other people's private property up close</strong> — backyards over a fence, through windows, or
          from a drone. (Colorado law also restricts drone photography of people in private places; see the
          <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>"Callout" photos</strong> — a neighbor's parking, trash cans, yard, pet, or a dispute. If something
          needs addressing, contact the HOA, the district, or the authorities instead.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Emergencies, accidents, injuries, or crime scenes.</strong>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Political, campaign, or religious messaging</strong> as the subject of the photo, or anything
          promotional — see our <a href="/site-info/neutrality-policy">Neutrality Policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Wildlife nests, dens, or burrows with a findable location,</strong> or animals being approached,
          fed, or disturbed for the shot.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Photos you didn't take</strong>, images with someone else's watermark, or AI-generated or heavily
          altered images presented as real.
        </li>
        <li>Anything graphic, explicit, hateful, or otherwise not suitable for all ages.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Editors have the final say and may decline any photo without giving a reason.</p>

      <h2>How to submit</h2>
      <p>
        Email your photo to <a href="mailto:bentgrassneighborhood@gmail.com?subject=Community%20Gallery%20photo">bentgrassneighborhood@gmail.com</a>
        with a short caption, roughly when it was taken, and whether you'd like credit (first name or initials
        only — we don't publish full names). By sending a photo, you confirm that:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>you took it yourself, and</li>
        <li>anyone recognizable in it (or their parent or guardian) is OK with it being posted.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You keep the copyright. You're giving us permission to show the photo on this site and in the newsletter
        for as long as this policy allows, and you can take that permission back at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do before posting</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Strip hidden data.</strong> Phone photos carry GPS coordinates and device details. We remove that
          data automatically from every gallery photo we store.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Resize, crop, or blur</strong> as needed to meet the rules above.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep photos</h2>
      <p>We don't want to store your photos forever, so everything has an expiration date:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Gallery photos:</strong> shown for up to {GALLERY_RETENTION_MONTHS} months from the day they're
          added. After that they're taken down and deleted from the site's files automatically. We check for
          expired photos every month.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your submission email and its attachments:</strong> deleted from our inbox within 30 days of
          posting the photo, or of deciding not to.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Photos we decline:</strong> never posted, and deleted within 30 days along with the email.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Photos used in a news post or event listing</strong> stay with that post. Ask and we'll swap
          one out at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Newsletters:</strong> once an issue is emailed we can't pull it back from inboxes, but we can
          remove a photo from the online archive.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        One honest caveat: this site's source code is public on GitHub, and GitHub keeps a version history of past
        changes. Deleted photos are no longer part of the site, but older copies can remain in that history. If you
        want a photo gone from there too, tell us and we'll take the extra steps to purge it.
      </p>

      <h2>Asking for a photo to come down</h2>
      <p>
        If you're in a photo, took a photo, or a photo shows your home or your kids, you can ask us to take it down
        — no reason needed. Email
        <a href="mailto:bentgrassneighborhood@gmail.com?subject=Photo%20removal">bentgrassneighborhood@gmail.com</a>
        with "Photo removal" in the subject and tell us which photo. We'll take it down within 7 days, and usually
        much sooner.
      </p>

      <h2>If things change</h2>
      <p>
        If we change these rules or how long we keep photos, we'll update this page and the date up top. Photos
        already posted follow whichever version is stricter.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
